1
00:00:00,597 --> 00:00:06,057
(GPS:)Three-digit route numbers
indicate bypasses or spurs.

2
00:00:07,971 --> 00:00:11,101
(Howard:)Look, Leonard, there's a bridge.
Drive off it.

3
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:14,665
(Raj:)You know, we're not that far
from Vasquez Rocks.

4
00:00:14,878 --> 00:00:17,938
(Sheldon:)Oh, they shot a lot of
Star Trek episodes out there.

5
00:00:18,181 --> 00:00:20,111
We got our costumes in the trunk...

6
00:00:20,317 --> 00:00:22,687
(Howard:)...we could go there
and have a little photo shoot.

7
00:00:22,886 --> 00:00:26,416
(Raj:)Great idea. I haven't had
a carbohydrate in two weeks.

8
00:00:26,623 --> 00:00:30,753
(Raj:)These cheekbones need to be in front of a
camera before I eat a pretzel and they're gone.

9
00:00:31,828 --> 00:00:34,458
- It sounds fun.
- Oh, smashing.

10
00:00:34,698 --> 00:00:36,958
(Sheldon:)Now, Leonard,
do you know how to get there?

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,070
(Sheldon:)- No.
- Yeah, well, luckily, someone in the car does.

12
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:42,300
(GPS:)Recalculating.

13
00:00:43,573 --> 00:00:46,473
(GPS:)While we're waiting,
do you know which president...

14
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:50,980
(GPS:)...signed the
Interstate Highway System Act into law?

15
00:00:51,214 --> 00:00:54,814
(GPS:)The answer coming up in 14 miles.

16
00:00:56,252 --> 00:01:13,032
(Sheldon:)None of you will get it. It's Eisenhower.

